--- reading it --------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. T046 holds. The RTC driver is built in, so it registers at 0.468 s and sets 2000-01-01
   before init; S00ota-clock then raises the clock to the build time (16:18:54, the same
   BUILD_DATE as /etc/build-info), and nothing overwrites it: `date` at the prompt reads
   16:19:10 on the same day. No `date -s` was typed. In the first boot the driver was a
   module and registered after the script, which is the whole difference.
2. T027 holds on the confirm path: "slot A confirmed good" and BOOT_A_LEFT back at 3 (the
   factory image starts it at 3; the boot above spent one, mark-good refilled it). The
   refuse paths and the last-resort path are still only host-tested.
3. Boot time is NOT measured here. The host timestamps have one-second resolution; SPL banner
   at 23:31:12 and login at 23:31:24 is about 12 s, against a budget of 12.65 s and a previous
   10.51 s (T025). That is close enough that T043 must re-measure with grabserial, three runs,
   rather than rely on this.
4. The network is not exercised: `Starting network: OK` brings up only lo, and no one ran
   udhcpc on eth0 yet. Delivery of a bundle (research R8) is still untested on hardware.
